I found the concrete environment defect: this sandbox reports a namespace-local PID via `getpid()` but its `/proc` mount exposes a different namespace. Lean 4.22 resolves its executable through `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, so both Lean and Lake fail before elaboration. I’ll use a narrowly scoped preload shim that redirects only those `/proc/<pid>/exe` `readlink` calls to `/proc/self/exe`, preserving the actual compiler and checker behavior. I’ll record the shim source, build, and rerun output.
